 "profile": {
  "what": "Broadcom designs chips for networking, data-centre connectivity, broadband, wireless and storage, and since buying VMware in 2023 it is also one of the largest enterprise software companies. It is a central supplier of the networking and custom AI chips that hyperscale cloud providers build their AI clusters around.",
  "money": "Two engines. Semiconductors (a little under 60% of fiscal 2025 revenue) sells chips to device makers and cloud giants, increasingly custom AI accelerators designed with a handful of very large customers. Infrastructure software (just over 40%) sells VMware, mainframe and security software on multi-year subscriptions with very high margins. Broadcom buys franchises, cuts costs hard and raises prices.",
  "valued": "The market prices Broadcom on forward earnings and free cash flow, and the multiple now rests on how fast its custom AI-chip business grows. Customer concentration in AI and the debt from VMware are the main reasons the multiple can fall.",
